      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The intrinsic haemolysis of an amyloid-β (Aβ) N-terminal targeting gramicidin S derivative was successfully dissociated from its Aβ oligomer-preventing activities via Ala-scanning-based regulation of molecular amphiphilicity. The representative analogue DGR-7 shows low toxicity but significant efficiency in preventing Aβ oligomers and reducing amyloid plaques in APP/PS1 transgenic AD mice."},
